    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 7,
    "title": "Present an event as a completed occurrence",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-perfective-le-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Present an event as a completed occurrence",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put 了 after a verb to present an occurrence as bounded. It is not a past-tense ending. It does not by itself prove that an intended result was achieved: reading a book and understanding it are different claims.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我去了朋友家。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ qù le péngyou jiā 。",
                "meaning": "I went to a friend’s home.",
                "audio": "2f40ef8c668cbabb4df8a0a8cacb60d5777774001674bb82a425bbe03d959320"
              },
              {
                "text": "我看了书，没看懂。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ kàn le shū ， méi kàndǒng 。",
                "meaning": "I read the book but did not understand it.",
                "audio": "fdaa2e668e3ad7adafff65560ab1c93d9c38f8b454b69663d6ff208a742b6f4b"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "了",
                "pinyin": "le",
                "meaning": "aspect or change-of-situation particle; not a past-tense ending",
